# Disable ALL line-ending conversion for this repository.
#
# This is not a style preference -- it protects a documented invariant.
# blockplan/core.py is frozen at exactly 44,044 bytes with LF endings. That
# byte count and its SHA-256 are recorded in backend/blockplan_service/paths.py
# (CORE_PY_BYTES, CORE_PY_SHA256) and asserted by
# backend/tests/test_frozen_artifacts.py, which is how the frozen core is
# proven not to have been altered.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true. Without the rule below, git would
# convert core.py's 1,003 LF endings to CRLF on checkout, making the file
# 45,047 bytes and breaking every integrity check that refers to it -- while
# `git status` still reported a clean tree. The frozen CSV artifacts carry the
# same risk.
#
# Do not remove this line.
* -text
